      "writtenOn": "2024-08-30T23:44:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This CL also broke keymint in main-swcar-dev \n\n[    5.073132] servicemanager: Caller(pid\u003d169,uid\u003d9999,sid\u003du:r:hal_keymint_default:s0) Could not find android.hardware.security.keymint.IKeyMintDevice/default in the VINTF manifest. No alternative instances declared in VINTF.",
      "revId": "cf0a2dd5b005fa9353f11e59839cf374bddd1e8b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4a26ca4_4316b6a8",
        "filename": "tv/tuner/aidl/default/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-26T20:42:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why this instead of:\n\n```\nvintf_fragments: [\n    \":tuner-default.xml\"\n],\n```\n\nOtherwise, I wonder what the difference is between `vintf_fragment_modules` and `required`. Why do we need the new field?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "cf0a2dd5b005fa9353f11e59839cf374bddd1e8b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61fab6f1_49fff44f",
        "filename": "tv/tuner/aidl/default/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1413436
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-27T02:07:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is discussed from https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/3183863/6..17/android/module.go#b502 . I decided to use `vintf_fragment_modules` instead of `required` because APEX exposes required of internal modules as APEX required itself - which means if we put this module as `required` then vintf_fragment file will be installed both in the APEX, and also partition contains APEX.",
      "parentUuid": "c4a26ca4_4316b6a8",
